[comment encoding = UTF-8 /]

[**
Module contains queries with a UML type as receiver.
This includes queries for retrieving the type name of both
regular types and UML primitive types, and for classifying
types as primitive or non-primitive.

Note: UML primitive types (String, Integer, Boolean, Real)
require special handling since their name property is not
directly accessible when loaded as proxies. The queries in
this module provide a uniform interface for all type name
retrieval regardless of whether the type is a primitive
or a regular classifier.

Related modules:
- classifierQuery: queries with a UML classifier as receiver,
  since Classifier is a subtype of Type
- classQuery: queries with a UML class as receiver
- dataTypeQuery: queries with a UML data type as receiver
/]
[module typeQuery(
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML',
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/Types',
	'http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/Profile/Standard'
)/]

[**
Returns the simple name of a UML type. For resolved types, returns
the name property directly. For unresolved UML primitive type proxies
(e.g. Boolean, Integer, String, Real from UMLPrimitiveTypes.xmi),
the name is extracted from the toString() representation since the
name property returns empty on unresolved proxies.
Note: this workaround is not necessary if UMLResourcesUtil.init(
resourceSet) is registered in the generator launcher, in which case
all primitive type proxies resolve correctly and name is always
accessible. The workaround degrades gracefully when registration
is present.
---
AQL operations used:
  aType.eClass().name              - AQL operation on EObject: returns
                                     the EMF metaclass name. Returns
                                     'PrimitiveType' for all
                                     uml::PrimitiveType instances,
                                     including unresolved proxies.
  aType.toString()                 - Returns the Java toString()
                                     representation of the type. For
                                     unresolved proxies this contains
                                     the proxy URI including the type
                                     name fragment after '#', e.g.:
                                     '...PrimitiveTypeImpl@x
                                     (eProxyURI: ...#Boolean)'.
  s.lastIndex('#')                 - Returns the index of the last
                                     occurrence of '#' in the string.
  s.substring(n)                   - Returns the substring from
                                     position n onwards.
  .replace('\\)','')               - Removes the trailing ')' from
                                     the extracted fragment using a
                                     regex escape.
  aType.name                       - EStructuralFeature on
                                     uml::NamedElement: returns the
                                     name of a resolved type directly.

@param aType - A UML type whose simple name is to be returned,
               including unresolved primitive type proxies.
/]
[comment] [query public u_typeName(aType : uml::Type) : String =
  if aType.eClass().name = 'PrimitiveType' then
    let s : String = aType.toString()
    in
      s.substring(s.lastIndex('#') + 1).replace('\\)', '')
  else
    aType.name
  endif
/]
[/comment]
[**
Returns the qualified name of a UML type. For resolved types, returns
the name property directly. For unresolved UML primitive type proxies
(e.g. Boolean, Integer, String, Real from UMLPrimitiveTypes.xmi),
the name is extracted from the toString() representation since the
name property returns empty on unresolved proxies.
Note: this workaround is not necessary if UMLResourcesUtil.init(
resourceSet) is registered in the generator launcher, in which case
all primitive type proxies resolve correctly and name is always
accessible. The workaround degrades gracefully when registration
is present.

@param aType - A UML type whose simple name is to be returned,
               including unresolved primitive type proxies.
/]
[comment] [query public u_typeQualifiedName(aType : uml::Type) : String =
  if aType.eClass().name = 'PrimitiveType' then
    let s : String = aType.toString()
    in
      s.substring(s.lastIndex('#') + 1).replace('\\)', '')
  else
    aType.qualifiedName
  endif
/]
[/comment]

[**
 * Checks whether a given UML type is one of the five standard UML
 * primitive types defined in the UML Primitive Types library
 * (Boolean, Integer, String, Real, UnlimitedNatural), as opposed to
 * a user-defined type.
 *
 * The check first guards that the type is actually a uml::PrimitiveType,
 * then compares the resource URI of the type against the known URI of
 * the UML Primitive Types library resource. This is more reliable than
 * a name-based check, since it is independent of user-defined types
 * that may share names with standard ones.
 *
 * Note: This query requires access to the element's containing resource
 * via eResource() and is therefore not expressible in pure AQL. A Java
 * service call is needed to resolve the resource URI.
 *
 * @param aType   The UML type to check (e.g. from a Property or Parameter).
 * @return        true if the type is a standard UML primitive type,
 *                false if it is user-defined or not a primitive type at all.
 */]
[query public u_isUmlPrimitive(aType : uml::Type) : Boolean =
  aType.oclIsKindOf(uml::PrimitiveType)
  and aType.eResource().getURI().toString()
  = 'pathmap://UML_LIBRARIES/UMLPrimitiveTypes.library.uml'
/]
